<h2>Desktops</h2>
<p>The M5 Ultra in the Mac Studio doubles up to 4 ProRes engines and 4 video encode engines—the best option for 8K multicam or high-volume ProRes rendering. The M5 Max is the sweet spot for most professional 4K–6K workflows, with two encode and two ProRes engines. The M6 in the Mac mini and the M4 in the iMac each carry a single video encode, decode, and ProRes engine — fine for casual editing, but they will bottleneck on heavier exports.</p>

